================================================================================
Forge-side code: clean-room
================================================================================
Forbric's Forge-compatibility code (the net.forbric.loader.impl.*.forge.*
packages and related Forge metadata / mapping / access / lifecycle code) is an
independent clean-room implementation written from public formats and
specifications (the mods.toml schema, JarInJar metadata, modern Forge
IEventBus/registry contracts, the Maven version-range grammar, and Mixin).

It does NOT contain any source code from Forge Mod Loader (FML). FML, which is
licensed under the GNU LGPL v2.1 or later, was consulted only as a behavioural
reference. See CREDITS.md.

================================================================================
Mappings
================================================================================
Forbric does NOT bundle MCP mapping data, which is non-redistributable.
Runtime mappings are generated from permitted sources only (Mojang official
mappings, Fabric intermediary, and Yarn). See MAPPINGS.md.

